<% content_for :page_title, "Comparing the Collections - #{application_name}" %>

<section class="site-section compare-collections-section blacklight-pages-api_access">
  <div class="container compare-collections-page api-access-page api-access-page--modern">
    <div class="compare-frame">
      <header class="api-hero">
        <div class="api-hero__grid api-hero__grid--single">
          <div class="api-hero__copy">
            <h1 class="section-title">
              <span class="api-hero__eyebrow-text">Canadiana Collections and Infrastructure</span>
              <span class="api-hero__title-main">Comparing the Collections</span>
            </h1>
            <p class="api-lede">Discover digitized publications and archival records from across Canada.</p>
            <p>
              CRKN provides access to two major digital heritage collections: the Canadiana Collection and the Heritage Collection.
              The Canadiana collections are one of the largest collections of digitized Canadian documentary heritage in the world.
              Available at no charge thanks to the ongoing support of CRKN members through the Heritage Content Access and Preservation (HCAP) fund,
              the collections offer millions of pages of heritage content to researchers around the globe.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="compare-hero-grid">
        <div class="compare-hero-spacer" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <article class="compare-collection-card">
          <img src="<%= asset_path('monog.jpg') %>" alt="Books and periodicals in the Canadiana Collection" loading="lazy">
          <div class="compare-collection-body">
            <h3>Canadiana Collection</h3>
            <p class="compare-collection-type">Published Heritage</p>
            <p class="compare-collection-metric">31M+ pages</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="compare-collection-card">
          <img src="<%= asset_path('heritage-manuscript.jpg') %>" alt="Archival documents in the Heritage Collection" loading="lazy">
          <div class="compare-collection-body">
            <h3>Heritage Collection</h3>
            <p class="compare-collection-type">Archival Microfilm</p>
            <p class="compare-collection-metric">60M projected (37.5M current)</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="compare-spec-scroll">
        <table class="compare-spec-table">
          <caption class="visually-hidden">Comparison of Canadiana and Heritage collections</caption>
          <colgroup>
            <col class="compare-col-feature">
            <col class="compare-col-value">
            <col class="compare-col-value">
          </colgroup>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">Feature</span></th>
              <th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">Canadiana Collection</span></th>
              <th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">Heritage Collection</span></th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="compare-spec-row" data-equal="false">
              <th scope="row">Primary focus</th>
              <td>Published Canadian heritage: books, serials, maps, and government publications.</td>
              <td>Archival microfilm records from Library and Archives Canada and partners.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="compare-spec-row" data-equal="false">
              <th scope="row">Date range</th>
              <td>c. 1500 to present day</td>
              <td>1600s to mid-1900s</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="compare-spec-row" data-equal="false">
              <th scope="row">Collection size</th>
              <td>Approximately 31 million pages</td>
              <td>Approximately 60 million pages projected (37 million pages current)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="compare-spec-row" data-equal="false">
              <th scope="row">Genealogy materials</th>
              <td>Limited</td>
              <td>Strong coverage, including family, immigration, and voters' records</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="compare-spec-row" data-equal="false">
              <th scope="row">Indigenous history</th>
              <td>Strong in published scholarship and commentary</td>
              <td>Strong in archival records and government files</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="compare-spec-row" data-equal="false">
              <th scope="row">Newspapers and magazines</th>
              <td><span class="compare-token compare-token--yes">Yes</span></td>
              <td><span class="compare-token compare-token--no">No</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="compare-spec-row" data-equal="false">
              <th scope="row">Maps</th>
              <td><span class="compare-token compare-token--yes">Yes</span></td>
              <td><span class="compare-token compare-token--no">No</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="compare-spec-row" data-equal="false">
              <th scope="row">Military records</th>
              <td>Selected published military histories</td>
              <td>Extensive military archival documentation</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="compare-spec-row" data-equal="true">
              <th scope="row">Access model</th>
              <td>Available through the Canadiana platform for CRKN member communities</td>
              <td>Available through the Canadiana platform for CRKN member communities</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="compare-spec-row" data-equal="false">
              <th scope="row">Best for</th>
              <td>Published source discovery, periodical research, and print culture analysis.</td>
              <td>Primary archival research, genealogy, and government documentary history.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="compare-spec-row compare-spec-row--action" data-equal="false">
              <th scope="row"><span class="visually-hidden">Browse now</span></th>
              <td><a class="compare-action-link" href="<%= about_canadiana_path(lang: I18n.locale) %>">Go to Canadiana <i class="bi bi-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></a></td>
              <td><a class="compare-action-link" href="<%= about_heritage_path(lang: I18n.locale) %>">Go to Heritage <i class="bi bi-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></a></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <section class="api-card mt-3">
        <p>
          As resources developed over decades of collecting and preserving documents, CRKN acknowledges that the Canadiana
          collections contain material that is offensive and biased, contributing to an incomplete, distorted, and harmful
          story of Canada. We are dedicated to redefining the principles guiding the collections, helping to ensure that
          future development is firmly grounded in our commitment to reconciliation and justice. Currently, CRKN is
          <a href="https://www.crkn-rcdr.ca/en/call-canadiana-collection-development-projects" target="_blank" rel="noopener">expanding the collection</a>
          with content from member and stakeholder collections while prioritizing at-risk materials, newspapers,
          and content that represents the diversity of the Canadian population.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-0">
          The Canadiana collections are overseen by the
          <a href="https://www.crkn-rcdr.ca/en/preservation-and-access-committee" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Preservation and Access Committee</a> (PAC)
          and the PAC's sub-committees, the
          <a href="https://www.crkn-rcdr.ca/en/canadiana-content-sub-committee-ccsc" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Canadiana Content Sub-Committee</a>
          and the
          <a href="https://www.crkn-rcdr.ca/en/platform-technical-sub-committee-ptsc" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Platform Technical Sub-Committee</a>.
          To learn more about the Canadiana
          collections, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@crkn.ca">info@crkn.ca</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
